Rig a static Workspace Model as an R15 avatar and place the result beside it.
Pass `instance_path` whenever the Model is known; omit it only to use the
user's single selected Model. Do not set Selection with execute_luau.
Usually takes 3-5 minutes.

Studio MCP Proxy - bridges MCP clients with Roblox Studio

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__Roblox_Studio__auto_setup_avatar(args: {
  // Fix the front to negative Z. Defaults to false, which lets the engine infer it. Use true for ambiguous models that already face negative Z.
  align_front_angle?: boolean;
  // Labels for Models and BaseParts under the input. A Model covers every BasePart inside it. Omit to let the engine decide. Unlisted parts become Body; an R15 body with a Humanoid is skipped.
  classifications?: Array<{
  // Body is the avatar itself. Layered is layered clothing, including shoes. EyeLayered is eyelashes or eyebrows. Rigid is a fixed accessory like a hat.
  classification: "Body" | "Layered" | "EyeLayered" | "Rigid";
  // Path under the input Model, such as "Acc.Staff_Rigid", or the full path from inspect_instance. A Model covers every BasePart inside it.
  path: string;
  // uniqueId from inspect_instance. Required only when path matches more than one instance.
  uniqueId?: string;
}>;
  // Create a dynamic head from a 2D face Decal or texture. Defaults to false.
  decal_to_dynamic_head?: boolean;
  // Align the head cage to facial features for a better makeup fit. Defaults to true.
  enable_additional_head_processing?: boolean;
  // Workspace path to the input Model, preferably from inspect_instance. Pass it whenever known; omit only for the user's single selected Model.
  instance_path?: string;
  // Add optional upper-torso, neck, hand, and foot joints for more articulation. Defaults to false.
  r15_plus?: boolean;
  // Development only: reduce triangles for validation. Defaults to false. Omit for Platform, which always reduces them.
  reduce_triangles?: boolean;
  // "Platform" (default) creates marketplace-compatible avatars. "Development" creates experience-only characters such as NPCs.
  setup_type?: "Platform" | "Development";
  // Selects Roblox Studio instance, use the list_roblox_studios tool to get available instances
  studio_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
